		{
			"id":"2c5d06a364b13a19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"creatures, when killed, turn into food which can be eaten to gain some ichor.\n\nichor should have a `try_steal()` function that attempts to steal ichor but if the entity has none it fails and if the actor has max then it fails. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":130,
			"width":360,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"5337b9a1c263e641",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"a main menu\n\nthe main menu should just be an already initialized game without the player\n\n(the camera should choose to focus on a randomly picked entity on the map)\n\nthere will only be an option to play again or turn on and off the shaders. (this is because this will be a demo copy)\n\n---\n\nit is written in `AppController` `enum AppStatus { MENU, GAME, GAMEOVER }`.\n**MENU** should have the main menu open and visible with hand visible and able to select various interactableui elements.\n\ntitle, play, shader settings. (this is a demo copy so no quit button)\n\nmake this:\n- UIStage (simply registers all of its interactableUI)\n\t- InteractableUI (multiple of these, triggers an event when the hand activates it)\n\nwhere a method on `Hand` `switch_to_stage(stage: UIStage)` correctly moves the hand to the first element in the stage. this will be useful for navigating through different menu screens.\n\nessentially, activate a new game but do not spawn the player.\n\nensure that the hand always follows the element in space that it has selected.\n\n**GAME** is when the player is spawned and fully in control.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2770,
			"y":-200,
			"width":710,
			"height":680
		},
